# WP1 perf-list: 20,000 synthetic rows (a sandbox prepared with the
# synth::corpus layout: 10 projects, 20k single-exchange sessions). Release
# build, DESIGN 15.8 targets (FEATURES S-037, X-008, X-009, X-010):
#   * UI-thread time per typed key <= 2 ms (list.ui_busy_max, milliseconds)
#   * the pane's share of the install at the end of the load <= 16 ms
#     (list.install_pane_max). The loader's share (list.loader_install_max) is
#     core's Browser install: reported, not asserted (CCR in the hand-off).
#   * holding PageDown / Down through the whole list keeps the frame p95 <= 16 ms
#     (the pane's and the main window's)
#   * the UUID below is typed (36 keystrokes, each one set_query): the worst
#     case of a paste; then pasted (one keystroke, `busy.paste` = the whole
#     UI-thread update of the paste <= 2 ms; integrator, Phase C).
wait-loaded 180s
expect list.total > 19000
timing list.install_pane_max < 16ms
type "synthetic"
wait 50ms
wait-for list.searching == false 10s
type " conversation 19"
wait 50ms
wait-for list.searching == false 10s
timing list.ui_busy_max < 2ms
key escape
# a typed UUID: the disk lookup runs in the background
type "00000000-1c2d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b"
wait 500ms
timing list.ui_busy_max < 2ms
key escape
# the same UUID pasted: one change event
# (judged by the median of three: one sample in twenty carries a UI-thread hiccup outside the handler)
paste "000003e8-1c2d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b"
wait-for list.count == 1 10s
expect list.selected_title == "Synthetic conversation 0"
key escape
wait 300ms
paste "000003e9-1c2d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b"
wait-for list.count == 1 10s
key escape
wait 300ms
paste "000003ea-1c2d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b"
wait-for list.count == 1 10s
timing busy.paste_median < 2ms
key escape
# hold PageDown / Down at the key-repeat pace (33 ms per press, X-008): 800
# pages walk the 20k rows end to end, 300 more presses move one row each. The
# pane's own build time (list.frame_p95) and the whole main-window frame
# (window.frame_p95, the last 512 frames: the pane plus the viewer and chrome)
# must both stay within the 16 ms frame budget.
wait 300ms
hold pagedown 800
hold down 300
key end
key home
timing list.frame_p95 < 16ms
timing window.frame_p95 < 16ms
quit 0
